The DRAWN regime, and the only group in this migration that is a pure rename.

rc290 removed the seed= parameter and rc292 removed the op, but the replacement
klein4_expand is the SAME computation: its body reproduces
random.Random(seed).randrange(4), which is exactly what the old seed= path ran.
So every research number computed through these 280 sites is preserved bit-exact.

That is asserted, not assumed:
  - klein4_expand(D, seed) compared against random.Random(seed).randrange(4)
    directly, over 240 (D, seed) combinations spanning D in {16,64,256,2048,8192}
    and the seed values this tree actually uses (0-39, 4242, 6000, 71000-71005,
    80010, 99001, 123456, 2**31-1). Zero mismatches.
  - all 152 touched files byte-compile.

Edits are AST-byte-spliced at exact call spans, so no line outside a call was
rewritten and CRLF endings are untouched: 274 insertions / 274 deletions, one
line changed per line containing a site.

The number-CHANGING groups are deliberately NOT in this commit.

